=[ Ordiola ]

Workspace document editor for Tomet with hybrid block and WYSIWYG editing, built on Tauri v2 and Svelte 5.

==[ Status ]

Ordiola is a personal project, built around my own workflow and preferences.

- Pull requests are welcome. Issues may or may not be addressed, depending on my mood and time.
- No stability guarantees: behavior, file formats, and extension APIs may change without notice.
- Features exist because I need them, not because they are expected of a notes app.

If you are looking for a stable, well-supported editor, I recommend Obsidian (https://obsidian.md) with Markdown.

==[ Features ]

- **Tomet Native**: Read and edit `.tmt` documents natively with AST-level preservation.
- **Dual Mode Editing**:
  - **Block Hybrid Mode**: Edit markup inline within structured blocks (<callout>, @meta, etc.).
  - **Full Block Mode (WYSIWYG)**: Seamless rich-text rendering with ProseMirror / Tiptap.
- **Workspace Navigation**: Browse and organize files in vaults.
- **Powered by Tauri v2 & Svelte 5**: Ultra-fast and lightweight desktop application.

==[ Development ]

===[ Prerequisites ]

- Nix with Flakes enabled (recommended)
- Rust toolchain (MSRV 1.85+)
- Node.js & pnpm
- WebKitGTK 4.1 & GTK3 development libraries (Linux)

===[ Using Nix Flake ]

```bash
`` direnv allow
`` # or
`` nix develop
```

===[ Running Locally ]

```bash
`` just frontend-install
`` just dev
```
